  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "v3s1_01",
      "text": "Hello, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the fascinating world of Supervised Learning."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_02",
      "text": "It's about teaching machines to learn from examples where the correct answer is already known."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_03",
      "text": "We provide a machine with two things: Inputs and their corresponding Labels."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_04a",
      "text": "Student marks and whether they passed or failed."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_04b",
      "text": "Email content — spam or not spam."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_04c",
      "text": "House features and the price it sold for."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_05",
      "text": "Can a machine learn the hidden rule behind these examples? Can it look at a new, unlabeled input and predict the correct label?"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_06",
      "text": "Sometimes the rule is given directly. Like — if a data point is on one side, classify it as orange. If it's on the other side, classify it as blue."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_07",
      "text": "But in Supervised Learning… the model itself learns this rule. It observes hundreds of examples, and then… it infers the underlying pattern."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_08a",
      "text": "Sometimes the answer is a category — like spam."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_08b",
      "text": "Other times, it is a continuous number — like a house price."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_08c",
      "text": "These two types lead us to Classification and Regression."
    },
    {
      "id": "v3s1_08d",
      "text": "Let's explore those next."
    }
  ],
